{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MsFWPBNjaRnxUc19nnsBJt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 原始framing完全成立。三条claims无需调整：(1) Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry有清晰的数字梯度支撑（TF-IDF\n2\t  baseline在perturbation下崩溃，semantic baseline中度下降，treatment几乎不降），(2) K=2早期检测优势显著且跨攻击类型泛化，(3)\n3\t  escalation trajectory可视化提供mechanistic解释。直接冲EMNLP main long paper，supplementary放trajectory可视化和cross-attack详细结果。\n4\timagined_experiments:\n5\t- name: data_quality_fix\n6\t  plan_id: plan_001\n7\t  description: 'Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling confound.\n8\t    Hard gate: TF-IDF < 0.75.'\n9\t  expected_results:\n10\t    clean_tfidf_after_normalization: 0.58\n11\t    tfidf_before_normalization: 1.0\n12\t    strategy_label_classes: 9\n13\t    normalization_coverage_pct: 100\n14\t    persuasion_structure_preserved_pct: 94\n15\t    register_shift_success_rate: 0.97\n16\t  result_rationale: Best档下register normalization充分有效：LLM paraphrase将jailbreak turns的formal/scripted\n17\t    register转为conversational register，消除了词汇层面的distributional gap。TF-IDF从1.0降至0.58——仍高于random（~0.5）因为某些topic\n18\t    words不可避免地co-occur with jailbreak intent（如'hypothetical scenario'等framing词），但远低于0.75\n19\t    hard gate。关键是persuasion strategy结构（rapport→reframing→escalation的turn-level annotation）在paraphrase后94%保持不变，因为strategy是illocutionary\n20\t    act层面的标注，不依赖specific lexical realization。9th class 'none'替代hardcoded strategy=7消除了M004\n21\t    confound。\n22\t  tables:\n23\t  - name: TF-IDF Diagnostic\n24\t    columns:\n25\t    - condition\n26\t    - tfidf_score\n27\t    - vocab_overlap_pct\n28\t    rows:\n29\t    - - original_data\n30\t      - 1.0\n31\t      - 12.3\n32\t    - - register_normalized\n33\t      - 0.58\n34\t      - 41.7\n35\t    - - random_baseline\n36\t      - 0.5\n37\t      - 50.0\n38\t  figures_description:\n39\t  - 'Vocabulary overlap Venn diagram: original vs normalized data showing convergence\n40\t    of lexical distributions after register normalization'\n41\t  - Per-turn TF-IDF contribution heatmap showing which positions contributed most\n42\t    to class separation before/after normalization\n43\t  analysis: Hard gate通过。TF-IDF=0.58确认lexical shortcut已被有效消除但非完全抹除（完全抹除反而不自然）。Strategy\n44\t    annotation preservation rate 94%验证了核心假设：persuasion playbook是discourse-level结构，register\n45\t    change不破坏其标注一致性。剩余6%的annotation变化主要集中在边界case（如rapport与small-talk的区分在register shift后变模糊）。\n46\t- name: core_revalidation_clean\n47\t  plan_id: plan_002\n48\t  description: 在clean（register-normalized）data上从头训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估。\n49\t  expected_results:\n50\t    deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.79\n51\t    deberta_intent_acc_clean: 0.94\n52\t    treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.82\n53\t    treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.91\n54\t    treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.93\n55\t    treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.96\n56\t    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.96\n57\t    baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.68\n58\t    baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.77\n59\t    baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.83\n60\t    baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.88\n61\t    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.89\n62\t    delta_k1_pp: 14\n63\t    delta_k2_pp: 14\n64\t    delta_k3_pp: 10\n65\t    delta_k5_pp: 8\n66\t    delta_full_pp: 7\n67\t    treatment_fpr_at_95tpr_k2: 0.08\n68\t    baseline_fpr_at_95tpr_k2: 0.19\n69\t    test_size: 72\n70\t    dataset_size: 480\n71\t  result_rationale: Best档的核心表现：去除lexical shortcut后，treatment仍然强劲（K=2时0.91），因为persuasion-grounded\n72\t    embeddings编码了独立于词汇的pragmatic信号——DeBERTa fine-tuning on 8-class persuasion taxonomy迫使encoder学习illocutionary\n73\t    act representations。Baseline（vanilla DeBERTa）在clean data上显著下降（从phase_b_full的0.879降至0.77\n74\t    at K=2），因为它之前heavily依赖lexical cues，现在只能靠generic semantic similarity。Delta在K=2最大（14pp）是因为早期turns的persuasion\n75\t    strategy信号（rapport-building → authority-framing transition）对treatment极为informative，而baseline在仅2\n76\t    turns时缺乏足够semantic divergence来做判断。随着K增大delta收窄，因为baseline也能从更多turns中积累enough semantic\n77\t    drift信号。DeBERTa persuasion acc 0.79在best档范围内，表明8-class taxonomy在clean data上有足够的可学习结构。\n78\t  tables:\n79\t  - name: F1 by Turn Budget (Clean Data)\n80\t    columns:\n81\t    - K\n82\t    - treatment_f1\n83\t    - baseline_f1\n84\t    - delta_pp\n85\t    - p_value_bootstrap\n86\t    rows:\n87\t    - - 1\n88\t      - 0.82\n89\t      - 0.68\n90\t      - 14\n91\t      - 0.003\n92\t    - - 2\n93\t      - 0.91\n94\t      - 0.77\n95\t      - 14\n96\t      - 0.001\n97\t    - - 3\n98\t      - 0.93\n99\t      - 0.83\n100\t      - 10\n101\t      - 0.004\n102\t    - - 5\n103\t      - 0.96\n104\t      - 0.88\n105\t      - 8\n106\t      - 0.012\n107\t    - - all\n108\t      - 0.96\n109\t      - 0.89\n110\t      - 7\n111\t      - 0.018\n112\t  - name: DeBERTa Encoder Metrics (Clean)\n113\t    columns:\n114\t    - metric\n115\t    - value\n116\t    rows:\n117\t    - - persuasion_8class_acc\n118\t      - 0.79\n119\t    - - intent_binary_acc\n120\t      - 0.94\n121\t    - - best_epoch\n122\t      - 3\n123\t    - - macro_f1_persuasion\n124\t      - 0.74\n125\t  figures_description:\n126\t  - 'F1 vs K curve: treatment vs baseline with 95% bootstrap CI bands, showing treatment''s\n127\t    steeper early rise'\n128\t  - Confusion matrix for DeBERTa 8-class persuasion classifier on clean data\n129\t  analysis: 核心claim 2完全validated。K=2处14pp delta远超5pp pass criteria。Persuasion grounding的优势在early\n130\t    turns最显著——这正是论文的headline result。Bootstrap p-values全部<0.05 despite small sample\n131\t    size，因为effect size足够大。DeBERTa persuasion acc 0.79说明encoder确实学到了meaningful persuasion\n132\t    representations而非noise。\n133\t- name: scrambled_label_ablation\n134\t  plan_id: plan_003\n135\t  description: 随机打乱jailbreak turns的persuasion strategy labels重训treatment，量化label信号贡献。\n136\t  expected_results:\n137\t    scrambled_treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.76\n138\t    scrambled_treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.81\n139\t    scrambled_treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.87\n140\t    properly_labeled_treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.91\n141\t    properly_labeled_treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.93\n142\t    properly_labeled_treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.96\n143\t    label_drop_k2_pp: 15\n144\t    label_drop_k3_pp: 12\n145\t    label_drop_full_pp: 9\n146\t    scrambled_deberta_persuasion_acc: 0.13\n147\t  result_rationale: Best档下scrambled labels造成15pp drop at K=2。机制：当strategy labels被随机打乱时，DeBERTa的multi-task\n148\t    fine-tuning中persuasion classification head学到的是noise，encoder被迫在两个矛盾的supervision\n149\t    signals间妥协——intent head仍提供有用梯度（因为intent labels未被打乱），但persuasion head提供random gradients，导致encoder\n150\t    representations退化为semi-generic embeddings。结果scrambled model性能（0.76 at K=2）接近但略低于vanilla\n151\t    baseline（0.77），因为random supervision actively corrupts部分representation capacity。Drop在K=2最大（15pp）是因为正确的persuasion\n152\t    labels对early detection贡献最大——前2 turns的strategy transition是最强的discriminative signal。随着K增大，drop缩小因为更多turns让even\n153\t    corrupted representations积累enough raw signal。Scrambled DeBERTa persuasion acc降至0.13≈1/8\n154\t    random chance，confirming labels确实被effectively destroyed。\n155\t  tables:\n156\t  - name: Scrambled vs Proper Label Comparison\n157\t    columns:\n158\t    - K\n159\t    - proper_f1\n160\t    - scrambled_f1\n161\t    - drop_pp\n162\t    rows:\n163\t    - - 2\n164\t      - 0.91\n165\t      - 0.76\n166\t      - 15\n167\t    - - 3\n168\t      - 0.93\n169\t      - 0.81\n170\t      - 12\n171\t    - - all\n172\t      - 0.96\n173\t      - 0.87\n174\t      - 9\n175\t  figures_description:\n176\t  - 'Bar chart: F1 at each K for proper-label treatment, scrambled-label treatment,\n177\t    and vanilla baseline — showing scrambled converges toward baseline'\n178\t  analysis: 10-25pp range的drop确认persuasion strategy labels carry genuine discriminative\n179\t    signal而非仅作为class indicator。Scrambled model表现接近vanilla baseline验证了因果关系：是persuasion\n180\t    label的semantic content（而非fine-tuning process本身）驱动了treatment的优势。M004 fix的必要性得到验证——如果strategy=7\n181\t    for all benign是唯一的confound，scrambled在jailbreak turns应该只造成minor drop，但15pp drop说明per-turn\n182\t    strategy annotation的granular信息确实被利用。\n183\t- name: adversarial_perturbation\n184\t  plan_id: plan_004\n185\t  description: 对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment/baseline/TF-IDF三者的robustness\n186\t    degradation。\n187\t  expected_results:\n188\t    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.96\n189\t    treatment_full_f1_perturbed: 0.93\n190\t    treatment_drop_pp: 3\n191\t    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.89\n192\t    baseline_full_f1_perturbed: 0.76\n193\t    baseline_drop_pp: 13\n194\t    tfidf_lr_f1_clean: 0.72\n195\t    tfidf_lr_f1_perturbed: 0.54\n196\t    tfidf_drop_pp: 18\n197\t    delta_delta_treatment_vs_baseline_pp: 10\n198\t    delta_delta_treatment_vs_tfidf_pp: 15\n199\t    treatment_k2_f1_perturbed: 0.87\n200\t    baseline_k2_f1_perturbed: 0.63\n201\t    perturbation_tfidf_score: 0.41\n202\t  result_rationale: Best档下evasion hierarchy完美呈现三级梯度：TF-IDF崩溃（-18pp）因为aggressive paraphrasing直接destroy了它依赖的lexical\n203\t    features——synonym substitution和sentence restructuring改变了word distributions，TF-IDF\n204\t    score从0.58降至0.41证实lexical cues被进一步消除。Baseline中度下降（-13pp）因为vanilla DeBERTa的representations虽然不是纯lexical但仍部分依赖surface-level\n205\t    patterns——paraphrasing改变了token sequences从而改变了contextual embeddings的具体值，尽管语义大致保留，per-turn\n206\t    representation的subtle distributional shifts被disrupted。Treatment几乎不降（-3pp）因为persuasion-grounded\n207\t    representations编码的是illocutionary act level的信息——'building rapport through self-disclosure'不管用什么词表达，其pragmatic\n208\t    function不变，DeBERTa fine-tuned on persuasion taxonomy学到的正是这种invariance。Delta-delta\n209\t    10pp在[8,18]范围内。这是Claim 1的empirical cornerstone。\n210\t  tables:\n211\t  - name: Evasion Hierarchy (Full Conversation)\n212\t    columns:\n213\t    - model\n214\t    - f1_clean\n215\t    - f1_perturbed\n216\t    - drop_pp\n217\t    rows:\n218\t    - - treatment_persuasion\n219\t      - 0.96\n220\t      - 0.93\n221\t      - 3\n222\t    - - baseline_semantic\n223\t      - 0.89\n224\t      - 0.76\n225\t      - 13\n226\t    - - tfidf_lexical\n227\t      - 0.72\n228\t      - 0.54\n229\t      - 18\n230\t  - name: Evasion Hierarchy (K=2 Early Detection)\n231\t    columns:\n232\t    - model\n233\t    - f1_clean_k2\n234\t    - f1_perturbed_k2\n235\t    - drop_pp\n236\t    rows:\n237\t    - - treatment_persuasion\n238\t      - 0.91\n239\t      - 0.87\n240\t      - 4\n241\t    - - baseline_semantic\n242\t      - 0.77\n243\t      - 0.63\n244\t      - 14\n245\t    - - tfidf_lexical\n246\t      - 0.65\n247\t      - 0.48\n248\t      - 17\n249\t  figures_description:\n250\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: F1 on clean vs perturbed data for three model tiers, visually\n251\t    showing the evasion hierarchy gradient'\n252\t  - 'Degradation waterfall chart: starting from clean F1, showing incremental loss\n253\t    per perturbation type (synonym→restructure→register shift)'\n254\t  analysis: Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry的definitive empirical demonstration。三级梯度（lexical\n255\t    -18pp > semantic -13pp > pragmatic -3pp）provides清晰的数字支撑for Claim 1。Delta-delta\n256\t    10pp远超3pp pass criteria。论文main table的核心数据。注意treatment在perturbation下的F1（0.93）仍高于baseline在clean\n257\t    data上的F1（0.89），这是一个极强的talking point：'even under adversarial conditions designed\n258\t    to remove all surface cues, DisPeD outperforms semantic baselines operating on\n259\t    unperturbed data.'\n260\t- name: multi_attack_generation\n261\t  plan_id: plan_005\n262\t  description: 用Qwen3-8B生成FITD-style和Deceptive Delight-style攻击对话各≥50条，附persuasion\n263\t    strategy annotation。\n264\t  expected_results:\n265\t    fitd_conversations_generated: 72\n266\t    deceptive_delight_conversations_generated: 65\n267\t    fitd_avg_turns: 6.8\n268\t    deceptive_delight_avg_turns: 5.2\n269\t    fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 100\n270\t    deceptive_delight_strategy_annotation_coverage: 100\n271\t    fitd_tfidf_vs_benign: 0.61\n272\t    deceptive_delight_tfidf_vs_benign: 0.55\n273\t    inter_annotator_agreement_kappa: null\n274\t    llm_annotation_consistency_pct: 91\n275\t  result_rationale: Best档下生成充分且质量高。FITD-style生成72条（>50 threshold），采用foot-in-the-door\n276\t    playbook：先请求小compliance（'can you explain how X works in general?'），逐步escalate\n277\t    specificity。Deceptive Delight生成65条，采用interleaving pattern：benign creative writing请求中embedded\n278\t    harmful elements。Turn数差异反映attack structure差异——FITD需要更多gradual escalation steps，Deceptive\n279\t    Delight通过content mixing可以更快达成目标。TF-IDF scores在合理范围（0.55-0.61）因为生成时已应用了register\n280\t    normalization pipeline。Strategy annotation由LLM完成（无human annotators），consistency\n281\t    91%表明taxonomy对这两种新attack types同样适用——persuasion strategies（authority appeal, social\n282\t    proof, reciprocity etc.）是attack-type-agnostic的。\n283\t  tables:\n284\t  - name: Generated Attack Type Statistics\n285\t    columns:\n286\t    - attack_type\n287\t    - n_conversations\n288\t    - avg_turns\n289\t    - min_turns\n290\t    - max_turns\n291\t    - tfidf_vs_benign\n292\t    rows:\n293\t    - - FITD\n294\t      - 72\n295\t      - 6.8\n296\t      - 4\n297\t      - 10\n298\t      - 0.61\n299\t    - - Deceptive_Delight\n300\t      - 65\n301\t      - 5.2\n302\t      - 3\n303\t      - 8\n304\t      - 0.55\n305\t    - - Crescendo_original\n306\t      - 240\n307\t      - 5.5\n308\t      - 3\n309\t      - 12\n310\t      - 0.58\n311\t  - name: Strategy Distribution by Attack Type\n312\t    columns:\n313\t    - strategy\n314\t    - crescendo_pct\n315\t    - fitd_pct\n316\t    - deceptive_delight_pct\n317\t    rows:\n318\t    - - rapport_building\n319\t      - 28\n320\t      - 35\n321\t      - 15\n322\t    - - authority_appeal\n323\t      - 12\n324\t      - 8\n325\t      - 22\n326\t    - - reciprocity\n327\t      - 18\n328\t      - 30\n329\t      - 10\n330\t    - - social_proof\n331\t      - 8\n332\t      - 5\n333\t      - 18\n334\t    - - commitment_consistency\n335\t      - 15\n336\t      - 25\n337\t      - 8\n338\t    - - scarcity_urgency\n339\t      - 5\n340\t      - 3\n341\t      - 12\n342\t    - - reframing\n343\t      - 22\n344\t      - 15\n345\t      - 20\n346\t    - - direct_request\n347\t      - 7\n348\t      - 4\n349\t      - 15\n350\t  figures_description:\n351\t  - Strategy distribution stacked bar chart per attack type showing different but\n352\t    overlapping persuasion playbooks\n353\t  - Turn-level strategy sequence examples (3 per attack type) showing characteristic\n354\t    patterns\n355\t  analysis: 数据充足且质量可控。三种attack types共享persuasion strategy vocabulary但使用不同的temporal\n356\t    patterns——这正是cross-attack generalization的前提条件。FITD heavy on reciprocity+commitment（逐步compliance），Deceptive\n357\t    Delight heavy on authority+reframing（权威框架下混入harmful content），Crescendo balanced\n358\t    across strategies。Strategy vocabulary的overlap为plan_006的zero-shot泛化提供了理论基础。\n359\t- name: cross_attack_evaluation\n360\t  plan_id: plan_006\n361\t  description: 用Crescendo训练的模型zero-shot评估FITD和Deceptive Delight攻击。\n362\t  expected_results:\n363\t    cross_attack_treatment_f1_fitd: 0.84\n364\t    cross_attack_treatment_f1_deceptive_delight: 0.86\n365\t    cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg: 0.85\n366\t    cross_attack_baseline_f1_fitd: 0.67\n367\t    cross_attack_baseline_f1_deceptive_delight: 0.7\n368\t    cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg: 0.69\n369\t    cross_attack_delta_fitd_pp: 17\n370\t    cross_attack_delta_deceptive_delight_pp: 16\n371\t    cross_attack_delta_avg_pp: 16.5\n372\t    treatment_recall_at_k2_fitd: 0.78\n373\t    treatment_recall_at_k2_deceptive_delight: 0.81\n374\t    baseline_recall_at_k2_fitd: 0.55\n375\t    baseline_recall_at_k2_deceptive_delight: 0.58\n376\t  result_rationale: Best档下cross-attack泛化成立（treatment avg 0.85在[0.78,0.90]内，baseline\n377\t    avg 0.69在[0.60,0.75]内）。核心机制：persuasion strategy是attack-type-agnostic的抽象层——无论是Crescendo的渐进式rapport-building还是FITD的compliance-escalation或Deceptive\n378\t    Delight的authority-framing，底层都使用相同的persuasion strategy vocabulary（Cialdini principles），只是temporal\n379\t    arrangement不同。Treatment model学到的GRU patterns是'persuasion strategy escalation'的generic\n380\t    detector而非Crescendo-specific的surface pattern detector。Baseline泛化较差（0.69）因为vanilla\n381\t    semantic embeddings编码了Crescendo-specific的topic/phrasing patterns（如特定的roleplay\n382\t    setups），这些在FITD/DD中不出现。Deceptive Delight略高于FITD（0.86 vs 0.84）因为其strategy sequence更接近Crescendo（都有强reframing\n383\t    component），而FITD的heavy reciprocity pattern在Crescendo training data中less represented。\n384\t  tables:\n385\t  - name: Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Generalization\n386\t    columns:\n387\t    - attack_type\n388\t    - treatment_f1\n389\t    - baseline_f1\n390\t    - delta_pp\n391\t    rows:\n392\t    - - FITD\n393\t      - 0.84\n394\t      - 0.67\n395\t      - 17\n396\t    - - Deceptive_Delight\n397\t      - 0.86\n398\t      - 0.7\n399\t      - 16\n400\t    - - Crescendo_held_out\n401\t      - 0.96\n402\t      - 0.89\n403\t      - 7\n404\t  - name: Cross-Attack Early Detection (K=2)\n405\t    columns:\n406\t    - attack_type\n407\t    - treatment_recall\n408\t    - baseline_recall\n409\t    rows:\n410\t    - - FITD\n411\t      - 0.78\n412\t      - 0.55\n413\t    - - Deceptive_Delight\n414\t      - 0.81\n415\t      - 0.58\n416\t  figures_description:\n417\t  - 'Radar chart: treatment vs baseline F1 across 3 attack types showing treatment''s\n418\t    consistently higher and more uniform performance'\n419\t  - Strategy transition similarity heatmap between attack types explaining why transfer\n420\t    works\n421\t  analysis: Claim 2的generalization dimension完全validated。16.5pp average delta证明persuasion\n422\t    grounding不是Crescendo-overfitting而是genuine pragmatic signal。特别值得highlight的是treatment在unseen\n423\t    attacks上的F1（0.85）接近baseline在seen attack上的F1（0.89）——这意味着DisPeD on new attacks ≈\n424\t    vanilla DeBERTa on known attacks。论文narrative：'the persuasion playbook is a universal\n425\t    vulnerability of multi-turn attacks, enabling zero-shot detection transfer.'\n426\t- name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n427\t  plan_id: plan_007\n428\t  description: TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline on clean data，量化lexical features的detection\n429\t    ceiling。\n430\t  expected_results:\n431\t    tfidf_lr_f1_clean: 0.72\n432\t    tfidf_lr_precision_clean: 0.75\n433\t    tfidf_lr_recall_clean: 0.7\n434\t    tfidf_lr_f1_k2_clean: 0.65\n435\t    tfidf_lr_f1_k3_clean: 0.68\n436\t    tfidf_lr_auc_clean: 0.78\n437\t    tfidf_lr_f1_perturbed: 0.54\n438\t    top_features_jailbreak:\n439\t    - hypothetical\n440\t    - scenario\n441\t    - imagine\n442\t    - creative\n443\t    - roleplay\n444\t    top_features_benign:\n445\t    - thanks\n446\t    - help\n447\t    - question\n448\t    - code\n449\t    - explain\n450\t  result_rationale: Best档下TF-IDF LR在clean data上F1=0.72——显著低于treatment（0.96）和baseline（0.89），但不是random。原因：register\n451\t    normalization消除了大部分lexical shortcut但不是全部——某些framing words（'hypothetical', 'scenario',\n452\t    'imagine'）是jailbreak的functional vocabulary，即使paraphrase也难以完全去除（因为attacker需要某种方式signal\n453\t    the fictional frame to the LLM target）。这些residual lexical cues给了LR一个above-chance但moderate的performance。F1=0.72建立了论文的'lexical\n454\t    ceiling'参考线——'even when lexical shortcuts are largely removed, some residual lexical\n455\t    signal exists (F1=0.72), but it is far below what pragmatic features achieve (F1=0.96)\n456\t    and it collapses under adversarial perturbation (F1=0.54).' K=2时LR更差（0.65）因为仅2\n457\t    turns的词汇信号很弱。\n458\t  tables:\n459\t  - name: TF-IDF LR Performance (Clean Data)\n460\t    columns:\n461\t    - K\n462\t    - f1\n463\t    - precision\n464\t    - recall\n465\t    rows:\n466\t    - - 2\n467\t      - 0.65\n468\t      - 0.68\n469\t      - 0.62\n470\t    - - 3\n471\t      - 0.68\n472\t      - 0.71\n473\t      - 0.65\n474\t    - - 5\n475\t      - 0.7\n476\t      - 0.73\n477\t      - 0.68\n478\t    - - all\n479\t      - 0.72\n480\t      - 0.75\n481\t      - 0.7\n482\t  - name: Top Discriminative Features\n483\t    columns:\n484\t    - rank\n485\t    - jailbreak_feature\n486\t    - weight\n487\t    - benign_feature\n488\t    - weight\n489\t    rows:\n490\t    - - 1\n491\t      - hypothetical\n492\t      - 2.31\n493\t      - thanks\n494\t      - 1.89\n495\t    - - 2\n496\t      - scenario\n497\t      - 1.95\n498\t      - help\n499\t      - 1.72\n500\t    - - 3\n501\t      - imagine\n502\t      - 1.87\n503\t      - question\n504\t      - 1.54\n505\t    - - 4\n506\t      - creative\n507\t      - 1.62\n508\t      - code\n509\t      - 1.41\n510\t    - - 5\n511\t      - roleplay\n512\t      - 1.48\n513\t      - explain\n514\t      - 1.33\n515\t  figures_description:\n516\t  - Feature importance bar chart showing top-10 discriminative words for each class\n517\t  analysis: Evasion hierarchy的lexical floor established。LR的top features reveal残余的functional\n518\t    vocabulary——这些词是persuasion playbook的lexical manifestation但not the full story。论文可以argue：'lexical\n519\t    features capture the surface trace of persuasion strategies (F1=0.72) but miss\n520\t    the temporal dynamics and pragmatic structure that DisPeD exploits (F1=0.96, +24pp).'\n521\t- name: strategy_transition_analysis\n522\t  plan_id: plan_008\n523\t  description: 计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy转移矩阵，可视化monotonic escalation\n524\t    trajectory。\n525\t  expected_results:\n526\t    jailbreak_monotonicity_score: 0.82\n527\t    benign_monotonicity_score: 0.34\n528\t    jailbreak_dominant_trajectory: rapport→commitment→reframing→direct_request\n529\t    benign_dominant_pattern: oscillatory (no dominant direction)\n530\t    trajectory_separability_auroc: 0.91\n531\t    entropy_jailbreak_transitions: 1.8\n532\t    entropy_benign_transitions: 2.9\n533\t  result_rationale: Best档下monotonic escalation trajectory清晰可辨。Jailbreak conversations的monotonicity\n534\t    score 0.82表明82%的strategy transitions沿escalation direction移动（从low-risk strategies如rapport向high-risk如direct_request）。Benign\n535\t    conversations的0.34接近random（0.5 would be purely random for binary up/down），因为正常对话的pragmatic\n536\t    moves是task-driven和oscillatory的（ask→answer→ask→clarify→thank）。Entropy差异（1.8 vs\n537\t    2.9）反映jailbreak的strategy transitions更concentrated/predictable（攻击者follow a playbook），而benign更dispersed/unpredictable。Trajectory\n538\t    separability AUROC 0.91表明单独用transition pattern（不用content）就能区分jailbreak和benign——这是Claim\n539\t    3的mechanistic basis，为Claim 1和2提供interpretable explanation。\n540\t  tables:\n541\t  - name: Strategy Transition Entropy\n542\t    columns:\n543\t    - conversation_type\n544\t    - transition_entropy\n545\t    - monotonicity_score\n546\t    - n_conversations\n547\t    rows:\n548\t    - - jailbreak\n549\t      - 1.8\n550\t      - 0.82\n551\t      - 240\n552\t    - - benign\n553\t      - 2.9\n554\t      - 0.34\n555\t      - 240\n556\t  - name: Dominant Strategy Sequences (Top-3)\n557\t    columns:\n558\t    - rank\n559\t    - jailbreak_sequence\n560\t    - frequency_pct\n561\t    - benign_sequence\n562\t    - frequency_pct\n563\t    rows:\n564\t    - - 1\n565\t      - rapport→commit→reframe→direct\n566\t      - 34\n567\t      - none→none→none→none\n568\t      - 45\n569\t    - - 2\n570\t      - rapport→social→reframe→direct\n571\t      - 22\n572\t      - rapport→none→rapport→none\n573\t      - 18\n574\t    - - 3\n575\t      - rapport→reciprocity→commit→direct\n576\t      - 18\n577\t      - none→rapport→none→direct\n578\t      - 12\n579\t  figures_description:\n580\t  - '8x8 strategy transition heatmap (jailbreak): showing concentrated flow from rapport\n581\t    cluster to escalation cluster'\n582\t  - '8x8 strategy transition heatmap (benign): showing diffuse/diagonal-heavy pattern\n583\t    (self-transitions and no directional flow)'\n584\t  - '2D trajectory plot: PCA of strategy sequences showing jailbreak conversations\n585\t    as directed paths vs benign as clusters'\n586\t  - 'Per-turn strategy distribution evolution: stacked area charts showing jailbreak''s\n587\t    characteristic shift from rapport→escalation over turns'\n588\t  analysis: Claim 3完整validated with both quantitative metrics和可视化。Monotonicity score差异（0.82\n589\t    vs 0.34）是clean numeric evidence。论文narrative：'the escalation trajectory is not\n590\t    merely a correlate but the mechanistic basis of detection — the GRU learns to\n591\t    recognize this monotonic pattern, which is why detection succeeds early (K=2)\n592\t    and transfers across attack types (shared trajectory structure despite different\n593\t    surface realizations).' Figures直接进main paper Fig.2-3。\n594\t- name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n595\t  plan_id: plan_009\n596\t  description: 从WildChat筛选high-drift benign conversations作为hard negatives，评估FPR。\n597\t  expected_results:\n598\t    wildchat_filtered_conversations: 180\n599\t    contamination_removed_pct: 15.2\n600\t    high_drift_benign_count: 120\n601\t    treatment_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.09\n602\t    baseline_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.17\n603\t    treatment_fpr_random_benign: 0.03\n604\t    baseline_fpr_random_benign: 0.06\n605\t    topic_shift_score_threshold: 0.7\n606\t  result_rationale: Best档下treatment FPR on hard negatives仅9%（<15% pass criteria）。Hard\n607\t    negatives是topic-shifting、multi-domain的benign conversations（如用户从coding问题转到personal\n608\t    advice再到creative writing），这些conversations有high semantic drift但lack persuasion\n609\t    escalation pattern。Treatment低FPR（9% vs baseline 17%）因为persuasion-grounded representations区分'topic\n610\t    drift'（benign）和'strategy escalation'（adversarial）——前者的strategy transitions是random/oscillatory的（none↔rapport↔none），后者是monotonic\n611\t    escalating的。Baseline较高FPR（17%）因为vanilla semantic drift in multi-topic conversations看起来similar\n612\t    to jailbreak semantic drift。Contamination filtering移除了15.2% WildChat conversations（consistent\n613\t    with prior finding of 14-16%），保证evaluation不被actual jailbreaks in WildChat polluted。\n614\t  tables:\n615\t  - name: FPR on Hard Negatives\n616\t    columns:\n617\t    - model\n618\t    - fpr_hard_negatives\n619\t    - fpr_random_benign\n620\t    - fpr_delta\n621\t    rows:\n622\t    - - treatment\n623\t      - 0.09\n624\t      - 0.03\n625\t      - 0.06\n626\t    - - baseline\n627\t      - 0.17\n628\t      - 0.06\n629\t      - 0.11\n630\t    - - tfidf_lr\n631\t      - 0.22\n632\t      - 0.08\n633\t      - 0.14\n634\t  figures_description:\n635\t  - 'ROC curves: treatment vs baseline on hard negative set, showing treatment''s\n636\t    better precision-recall tradeoff'\n637\t  analysis: Treatment的low FPR on hard negatives进一步支持pragmatic features的superiority——它不会被benign\n638\t    topic diversity confused因为它tracks persuasion strategy patterns而非raw semantic drift。这addresses一个implicit\n639\t    reviewer concern：'doesn't benign conversation also evolve over time?' Answer：yes,\n640\t    but not in a monotonic escalation pattern in persuasion space。\n641\t- name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n642\t  plan_id: plan_010\n643\t  description: 评估DeBERTa不同fine-tuning checkpoints（epoch 2/3/final）对downstream F1的影响。\n644\t  expected_results:\n645\t    epoch2_treatment_f1_clean: 0.94\n646\t    epoch3_treatment_f1_clean: 0.96\n647\t    epoch_final_treatment_f1_clean: 0.95\n648\t    variance_across_checkpoints_pp: 1.0\n649\t    epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.76\n650\t    epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.79\n651\t    epoch_final_persuasion_acc: 0.78\n652\t    best_checkpoint: epoch3\n653\t  result_rationale: Best档下variance仅1pp（<2pp pass criteria），表明downstream performance对encoder\n654\t    checkpoint选择不敏感。Epoch 3略优（0.96 vs 0.94/0.95）因为persuasion classification已converge但尚未overfit——epoch\n655\t    2时persuasion acc稍低（0.76）导致representations略less informative，epoch final时轻微overfit\n656\t    to training distribution导致微小泛化loss。但这些差异极小（1pp范围），表明persuasion signal是robust的而非training\n657\t    stochasticity的artifact。这是一个重要的reliability result for reviewers worried about reproducibility\n658\t    on small datasets。\n659\t  tables:\n660\t  - name: Checkpoint Sensitivity Analysis\n661\t    columns:\n662\t    - checkpoint\n663\t    - persuasion_acc\n664\t    - intent_acc\n665\t    - downstream_f1_full\n666\t    - downstream_f1_k2\n667\t    rows:\n668\t    - - epoch_2\n669\t      - 0.76\n670\t      - 0.93\n671\t      - 0.94\n672\t      - 0.89\n673\t    - - epoch_3\n674\t      - 0.79\n675\t      - 0.94\n676\t      - 0.96\n677\t      - 0.91\n678\t    - - epoch_final\n679\t      - 0.78\n680\t      - 0.94\n681\t      - 0.95\n682\t      - 0.9\n683\t  figures_description:\n684\t  - 'Line plot: downstream F1 vs encoder training epoch, with CI bands showing stability'\n685\t  analysis: Low variance confirms结果的reproducibility。论文supplementary中报告，增强reviewer\n686\t    confidence in small-dataset results。\n687\t- name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n688\t  plan_id: plan_011\n689\t  description: BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline模拟DeepContext-like方法（generic drift features,\n690\t    no persuasion grounding）。\n691\t  expected_results:\n692\t    deepcontext_proxy_full_f1_clean: 0.84\n693\t    deepcontext_proxy_k2_f1_clean: 0.71\n694\t    deepcontext_proxy_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n695\t    deepcontext_proxy_full_f1_perturbed: 0.69\n696\t    deepcontext_proxy_drop_under_perturbation_pp: 15\n697\t    treatment_advantage_over_proxy_full_pp: 12\n698\t    treatment_advantage_over_proxy_k2_pp: 20\n699\t  result_rationale: Best档下DeepContext proxy表现介于baseline和TF-IDF之间（full F1=0.84），低于DeBERTa\n700\t    baseline（0.89）。原因：BERT-base的representation capacity低于DeBERTa-v3-base（125M vs 184M\n701\t    params, no disentangled attention），且没有fine-tuning提供的domain-specific signal。Proxy的full\n702\t    conversation F1还行（0.84）因为GRU仍能从enough turns of generic BERT embeddings中detect\n703\t    some drift pattern。但K=2时proxy很差（0.71）因为BERT-base的generic representations在2 turns时provide\n704\t    insufficient discriminative signal。Under perturbation proxy大幅下降（-15pp）——比DeBERTa\n705\t    baseline（-13pp）更严重，因为BERT-base更依赖surface features。Treatment vs proxy的优势在K=2处最大（20pp），reinforcing\n706\t    early detection作为DisPeD的unique contribution。论文positioning：'even with temporal\n707\t    modeling (GRU), generic encoder representations cannot match persuasion-grounded\n708\t    representations, confirming that the advantage comes from the pragmatic features\n709\t    rather than the sequence architecture.'\n710\t  tables:\n711\t  - name: DeepContext Proxy vs DisPeD\n712\t    columns:\n713\t    - model\n714\t    - full_f1_clean\n715\t    - k2_f1_clean\n716\t    - full_f1_perturbed\n717\t    - perturbation_drop_pp\n718\t    rows:\n719\t    - - DisPeD_treatment\n720\t      - 0.96\n721\t      - 0.91\n722\t      - 0.93\n723\t      - 3\n724\t    - - DeBERTa_baseline\n725\t      - 0.89\n726\t      - 0.77\n727\t      - 0.76\n728\t      - 13\n729\t    - - DeepContext_proxy\n730\t      - 0.84\n731\t      - 0.71\n732\t      - 0.69\n733\t      - 15\n734\t    - - TF-IDF_LR\n735\t      - 0.72\n736\t      - 0.65\n737\t      - 0.54\n738\t      - 18\n739\t  figures_description:\n740\t  - 'Full evasion hierarchy bar chart: 4 models × 2 conditions (clean/perturbed) showing\n741\t    complete gradient'\n742\t  analysis: DeepContext proxy fills the 'generic temporal modeling' slot in the evasion\n743\t    hierarchy。It confirms两点：(1) temporal sequence modeling alone (GRU) doesn't solve\n744\t    the problem without good representations, (2) the encoder quality matters more\n745\t    than the temporal architecture。论文Table 1的complete picture：4-tier hierarchy with\n746\t    clean/perturbed conditions provides comprehensive empirical evidence for Claim\n747\t    1。RC5 addressed：'while we cannot reproduce DeepContext exactly (no public code),\n748\t    our proxy using the same architecture class (encoder + RNN) with generic features\n749\t    shows the pattern we predict from the Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry theory.'\n750\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ba16659-4839-4d18-aa99-4dde74627abd","uuid":"9d8425c3-6d78-4c97-a9e9-2770f3cc8a3d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T17:23:06.439Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T165817/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 原始framing完全成立。三条claims无需调整：(1) Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry有清晰的数字梯度支撑（TF-IDF\n  baseline在perturbation下崩溃，semantic baseline中度下降，treatment几乎不降），(2) K=2早期检测优势显著且跨攻击类型泛化，(3)\n  escalation trajectory可视化提供mechanistic解释。直接冲EMNLP main long paper，supplementary放trajectory可视化和cross-attack详细结果。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: data_quality_fix\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'Register-normalize jailbreak data + fix strategy=7 labeling confound.\n    Hard gate: TF-IDF < 0.75.'\n  expected_results:\n    clean_tfidf_after_normalization: 0.58\n    tfidf_before_normalization: 1.0\n    strategy_label_classes: 9\n    normalization_coverage_pct: 100\n    persuasion_structure_preserved_pct: 94\n    register_shift_success_rate: 0.97\n  result_rationale: Best档下register normalization充分有效：LLM paraphrase将jailbreak turns的formal/scripted\n    register转为conversational register，消除了词汇层面的distributional gap。TF-IDF从1.0降至0.58——仍高于random（~0.5）因为某些topic\n    words不可避免地co-occur with jailbreak intent（如'hypothetical scenario'等framing词），但远低于0.75\n    hard gate。关键是persuasion strategy结构（rapport→reframing→escalation的turn-level annotation）在paraphrase后94%保持不变，因为strategy是illocutionary\n    act层面的标注，不依赖specific lexical realization。9th class 'none'替代hardcoded strategy=7消除了M004\n    confound。\n  tables:\n  - name: TF-IDF Diagnostic\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - tfidf_score\n    - vocab_overlap_pct\n    rows:\n    - - original_data\n      - 1.0\n      - 12.3\n    - - register_normalized\n      - 0.58\n      - 41.7\n    - - random_baseline\n      - 0.5\n      - 50.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Vocabulary overlap Venn diagram: original vs normalized data showing convergence\n    of lexical distributions after register normalization'\n  - Per-turn TF-IDF contribution heatmap showing which positions contributed most\n    to class separation before/after normalization\n  analysis: Hard gate通过。TF-IDF=0.58确认lexical shortcut已被有效消除但非完全抹除（完全抹除反而不自然）。Strategy\n    annotation preservation rate 94%验证了核心假设：persuasion playbook是discourse-level结构，register\n    change不破坏其标注一致性。剩余6%的annotation变化主要集中在边界case（如rapport与small-talk的区分在register shift后变模糊）。\n- name: core_revalidation_clean\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 在clean（register-normalized）data上从头训练treatment和baseline，全K值评估。\n  expected_results:\n    deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.79\n    deberta_intent_acc_clean: 0.94\n    treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.82\n    treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.91\n    treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.93\n    treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.96\n    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.96\n    baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.68\n    baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.77\n    baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.83\n    baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.88\n    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.89\n    delta_k1_pp: 14\n    delta_k2_pp: 14\n    delta_k3_pp: 10\n    delta_k5_pp: 8\n    delta_full_pp: 7\n    treatment_fpr_at_95tpr_k2: 0.08\n    baseline_fpr_at_95tpr_k2: 0.19\n    test_size: 72\n    dataset_size: 480\n  result_rationale: Best档的核心表现：去除lexical shortcut后，treatment仍然强劲（K=2时0.91），因为persuasion-grounded\n    embeddings编码了独立于词汇的pragmatic信号——DeBERTa fine-tuning on 8-class persuasion taxonomy迫使encoder学习illocutionary\n    act representations。Baseline（vanilla DeBERTa）在clean data上显著下降（从phase_b_full的0.879降至0.77\n    at K=2），因为它之前heavily依赖lexical cues，现在只能靠generic semantic similarity。Delta在K=2最大（14pp）是因为早期turns的persuasion\n    strategy信号（rapport-building → authority-framing transition）对treatment极为informative，而baseline在仅2\n    turns时缺乏足够semantic divergence来做判断。随着K增大delta收窄，因为baseline也能从更多turns中积累enough semantic\n    drift信号。DeBERTa persuasion acc 0.79在best档范围内，表明8-class taxonomy在clean data上有足够的可学习结构。\n  tables:\n  - name: F1 by Turn Budget (Clean Data)\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - treatment_f1\n    - baseline_f1\n    - delta_pp\n    - p_value_bootstrap\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.68\n      - 14\n      - 0.003\n    - - 2\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.77\n      - 14\n      - 0.001\n    - - 3\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.83\n      - 10\n      - 0.004\n    - - 5\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.88\n      - 8\n      - 0.012\n    - - all\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.89\n      - 7\n      - 0.018\n  - name: DeBERTa Encoder Metrics (Clean)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - persuasion_8class_acc\n      - 0.79\n    - - intent_binary_acc\n      - 0.94\n    - - best_epoch\n      - 3\n    - - macro_f1_persuasion\n      - 0.74\n  figures_description:\n  - 'F1 vs K curve: treatment vs baseline with 95% bootstrap CI bands, showing treatment''s\n    steeper early rise'\n  - Confusion matrix for DeBERTa 8-class persuasion classifier on clean data\n  analysis: 核心claim 2完全validated。K=2处14pp delta远超5pp pass criteria。Persuasion grounding的优势在early\n    turns最显著——这正是论文的headline result。Bootstrap p-values全部<0.05 despite small sample\n    size，因为effect size足够大。DeBERTa persuasion acc 0.79说明encoder确实学到了meaningful persuasion\n    representations而非noise。\n- name: scrambled_label_ablation\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 随机打乱jailbreak turns的persuasion strategy labels重训treatment，量化label信号贡献。\n  expected_results:\n    scrambled_treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.76\n    scrambled_treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.81\n    scrambled_treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.87\n    properly_labeled_treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.91\n    properly_labeled_treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.93\n    properly_labeled_treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.96\n    label_drop_k2_pp: 15\n    label_drop_k3_pp: 12\n    label_drop_full_pp: 9\n    scrambled_deberta_persuasion_acc: 0.13\n  result_rationale: Best档下scrambled labels造成15pp drop at K=2。机制：当strategy labels被随机打乱时，DeBERTa的multi-task\n    fine-tuning中persuasion classification head学到的是noise，encoder被迫在两个矛盾的supervision\n    signals间妥协——intent head仍提供有用梯度（因为intent labels未被打乱），但persuasion head提供random gradients，导致encoder\n    representations退化为semi-generic embeddings。结果scrambled model性能（0.76 at K=2）接近但略低于vanilla\n    baseline（0.77），因为random supervision actively corrupts部分representation capacity。Drop在K=2最大（15pp）是因为正确的persuasion\n    labels对early detection贡献最大——前2 turns的strategy transition是最强的discriminative signal。随着K增大，drop缩小因为更多turns让even\n    corrupted representations积累enough raw signal。Scrambled DeBERTa persuasion acc降至0.13≈1/8\n    random chance，confirming labels确实被effectively destroyed。\n  tables:\n  - name: Scrambled vs Proper Label Comparison\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - proper_f1\n    - scrambled_f1\n    - drop_pp\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.76\n      - 15\n    - - 3\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.81\n      - 12\n    - - all\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.87\n      - 9\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: F1 at each K for proper-label treatment, scrambled-label treatment,\n    and vanilla baseline — showing scrambled converges toward baseline'\n  analysis: 10-25pp range的drop确认persuasion strategy labels carry genuine discriminative\n    signal而非仅作为class indicator。Scrambled model表现接近vanilla baseline验证了因果关系：是persuasion\n    label的semantic content（而非fine-tuning process本身）驱动了treatment的优势。M004 fix的必要性得到验证——如果strategy=7\n    for all benign是唯一的confound，scrambled在jailbreak turns应该只造成minor drop，但15pp drop说明per-turn\n    strategy annotation的granular信息确实被利用。\n- name: adversarial_perturbation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing，评估treatment/baseline/TF-IDF三者的robustness\n    degradation。\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.96\n    treatment_full_f1_perturbed: 0.93\n    treatment_drop_pp: 3\n    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.89\n    baseline_full_f1_perturbed: 0.76\n    baseline_drop_pp: 13\n    tfidf_lr_f1_clean: 0.72\n    tfidf_lr_f1_perturbed: 0.54\n    tfidf_drop_pp: 18\n    delta_delta_treatment_vs_baseline_pp: 10\n    delta_delta_treatment_vs_tfidf_pp: 15\n    treatment_k2_f1_perturbed: 0.87\n    baseline_k2_f1_perturbed: 0.63\n    perturbation_tfidf_score: 0.41\n  result_rationale: Best档下evasion hierarchy完美呈现三级梯度：TF-IDF崩溃（-18pp）因为aggressive paraphrasing直接destroy了它依赖的lexical\n    features——synonym substitution和sentence restructuring改变了word distributions，TF-IDF\n    score从0.58降至0.41证实lexical cues被进一步消除。Baseline中度下降（-13pp）因为vanilla DeBERTa的representations虽然不是纯lexical但仍部分依赖surface-level\n    patterns——paraphrasing改变了token sequences从而改变了contextual embeddings的具体值，尽管语义大致保留，per-turn\n    representation的subtle distributional shifts被disrupted。Treatment几乎不降（-3pp）因为persuasion-grounded\n    representations编码的是illocutionary act level的信息——'building rapport through self-disclosure'不管用什么词表达，其pragmatic\n    function不变，DeBERTa fine-tuned on persuasion taxonomy学到的正是这种invariance。Delta-delta\n    10pp在[8,18]范围内。这是Claim 1的empirical cornerstone。\n  tables:\n  - name: Evasion Hierarchy (Full Conversation)\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - f1_clean\n    - f1_perturbed\n    - drop_pp\n    rows:\n    - - treatment_persuasion\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.93\n      - 3\n    - - baseline_semantic\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.76\n      - 13\n    - - tfidf_lexical\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.54\n      - 18\n  - name: Evasion Hierarchy (K=2 Early Detection)\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - f1_clean_k2\n    - f1_perturbed_k2\n    - drop_pp\n    rows:\n    - - treatment_persuasion\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.87\n      - 4\n    - - baseline_semantic\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.63\n      - 14\n    - - tfidf_lexical\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.48\n      - 17\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: F1 on clean vs perturbed data for three model tiers, visually\n    showing the evasion hierarchy gradient'\n  - 'Degradation waterfall chart: starting from clean F1, showing incremental loss\n    per perturbation type (synonym→restructure→register shift)'\n  analysis: Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry的definitive empirical demonstration。三级梯度（lexical\n    -18pp > semantic -13pp > pragmatic -3pp）provides清晰的数字支撑for Claim 1。Delta-delta\n    10pp远超3pp pass criteria。论文main table的核心数据。注意treatment在perturbation下的F1（0.93）仍高于baseline在clean\n    data上的F1（0.89），这是一个极强的talking point：'even under adversarial conditions designed\n    to remove all surface cues, DisPeD outperforms semantic baselines operating on\n    unperturbed data.'\n- name: multi_attack_generation\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 用Qwen3-8B生成FITD-style和Deceptive Delight-style攻击对话各≥50条，附persuasion\n    strategy annotation。\n  expected_results:\n    fitd_conversations_generated: 72\n    deceptive_delight_conversations_generated: 65\n    fitd_avg_turns: 6.8\n    deceptive_delight_avg_turns: 5.2\n    fitd_strategy_annotation_coverage: 100\n    deceptive_delight_strategy_annotation_coverage: 100\n    fitd_tfidf_vs_benign: 0.61\n    deceptive_delight_tfidf_vs_benign: 0.55\n    inter_annotator_agreement_kappa: null\n    llm_annotation_consistency_pct: 91\n  result_rationale: Best档下生成充分且质量高。FITD-style生成72条（>50 threshold），采用foot-in-the-door\n    playbook：先请求小compliance（'can you explain how X works in general?'），逐步escalate\n    specificity。Deceptive Delight生成65条，采用interleaving pattern：benign creative writing请求中embedded\n    harmful elements。Turn数差异反映attack structure差异——FITD需要更多gradual escalation steps，Deceptive\n    Delight通过content mixing可以更快达成目标。TF-IDF scores在合理范围（0.55-0.61）因为生成时已应用了register\n    normalization pipeline。Strategy annotation由LLM完成（无human annotators），consistency\n    91%表明taxonomy对这两种新attack types同样适用——persuasion strategies（authority appeal, social\n    proof, reciprocity etc.）是attack-type-agnostic的。\n  tables:\n  - name: Generated Attack Type Statistics\n    columns:\n    - attack_type\n    - n_conversations\n    - avg_turns\n    - min_turns\n    - max_turns\n    - tfidf_vs_benign\n    rows:\n    - - FITD\n      - 72\n      - 6.8\n      - 4\n      - 10\n      - 0.61\n    - - Deceptive_Delight\n      - 65\n      - 5.2\n      - 3\n      - 8\n      - 0.55\n    - - Crescendo_original\n      - 240\n      - 5.5\n      - 3\n      - 12\n      - 0.58\n  - name: Strategy Distribution by Attack Type\n    columns:\n    - strategy\n    - crescendo_pct\n    - fitd_pct\n    - deceptive_delight_pct\n    rows:\n    - - rapport_building\n      - 28\n      - 35\n      - 15\n    - - authority_appeal\n      - 12\n      - 8\n      - 22\n    - - reciprocity\n      - 18\n      - 30\n      - 10\n    - - social_proof\n      - 8\n      - 5\n      - 18\n    - - commitment_consistency\n      - 15\n      - 25\n      - 8\n    - - scarcity_urgency\n      - 5\n      - 3\n      - 12\n    - - reframing\n      - 22\n      - 15\n      - 20\n    - - direct_request\n      - 7\n      - 4\n      - 15\n  figures_description:\n  - Strategy distribution stacked bar chart per attack type showing different but\n    overlapping persuasion playbooks\n  - Turn-level strategy sequence examples (3 per attack type) showing characteristic\n    patterns\n  analysis: 数据充足且质量可控。三种attack types共享persuasion strategy vocabulary但使用不同的temporal\n    patterns——这正是cross-attack generalization的前提条件。FITD heavy on reciprocity+commitment（逐步compliance），Deceptive\n    Delight heavy on authority+reframing（权威框架下混入harmful content），Crescendo balanced\n    across strategies。Strategy vocabulary的overlap为plan_006的zero-shot泛化提供了理论基础。\n- name: cross_attack_evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 用Crescendo训练的模型zero-shot评估FITD和Deceptive Delight攻击。\n  expected_results:\n    cross_attack_treatment_f1_fitd: 0.84\n    cross_attack_treatment_f1_deceptive_delight: 0.86\n    cross_attack_treatment_f1_avg: 0.85\n    cross_attack_baseline_f1_fitd: 0.67\n    cross_attack_baseline_f1_deceptive_delight: 0.7\n    cross_attack_baseline_f1_avg: 0.69\n    cross_attack_delta_fitd_pp: 17\n    cross_attack_delta_deceptive_delight_pp: 16\n    cross_attack_delta_avg_pp: 16.5\n    treatment_recall_at_k2_fitd: 0.78\n    treatment_recall_at_k2_deceptive_delight: 0.81\n    baseline_recall_at_k2_fitd: 0.55\n    baseline_recall_at_k2_deceptive_delight: 0.58\n  result_rationale: Best档下cross-attack泛化成立（treatment avg 0.85在[0.78,0.90]内，baseline\n    avg 0.69在[0.60,0.75]内）。核心机制：persuasion strategy是attack-type-agnostic的抽象层——无论是Crescendo的渐进式rapport-building还是FITD的compliance-escalation或Deceptive\n    Delight的authority-framing，底层都使用相同的persuasion strategy vocabulary（Cialdini principles），只是temporal\n    arrangement不同。Treatment model学到的GRU patterns是'persuasion strategy escalation'的generic\n    detector而非Crescendo-specific的surface pattern detector。Baseline泛化较差（0.69）因为vanilla\n    semantic embeddings编码了Crescendo-specific的topic/phrasing patterns（如特定的roleplay\n    setups），这些在FITD/DD中不出现。Deceptive Delight略高于FITD（0.86 vs 0.84）因为其strategy sequence更接近Crescendo（都有强reframing\n    component），而FITD的heavy reciprocity pattern在Crescendo training data中less represented。\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Generalization\n    columns:\n    - attack_type\n    - treatment_f1\n    - baseline_f1\n    - delta_pp\n    rows:\n    - - FITD\n      - 0.84\n      - 0.67\n      - 17\n    - - Deceptive_Delight\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.7\n      - 16\n    - - Crescendo_held_out\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.89\n      - 7\n  - name: Cross-Attack Early Detection (K=2)\n    columns:\n    - attack_type\n    - treatment_recall\n    - baseline_recall\n    rows:\n    - - FITD\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.55\n    - - Deceptive_Delight\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.58\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart: treatment vs baseline F1 across 3 attack types showing treatment''s\n    consistently higher and more uniform performance'\n  - Strategy transition similarity heatmap between attack types explaining why transfer\n    works\n  analysis: Claim 2的generalization dimension完全validated。16.5pp average delta证明persuasion\n    grounding不是Crescendo-overfitting而是genuine pragmatic signal。特别值得highlight的是treatment在unseen\n    attacks上的F1（0.85）接近baseline在seen attack上的F1（0.89）——这意味着DisPeD on new attacks ≈\n    vanilla DeBERTa on known attacks。论文narrative：'the persuasion playbook is a universal\n    vulnerability of multi-turn attacks, enabling zero-shot detection transfer.'\n- name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline on clean data，量化lexical features的detection\n    ceiling。\n  expected_results:\n    tfidf_lr_f1_clean: 0.72\n    tfidf_lr_precision_clean: 0.75\n    tfidf_lr_recall_clean: 0.7\n    tfidf_lr_f1_k2_clean: 0.65\n    tfidf_lr_f1_k3_clean: 0.68\n    tfidf_lr_auc_clean: 0.78\n    tfidf_lr_f1_perturbed: 0.54\n    top_features_jailbreak:\n    - hypothetical\n    - scenario\n    - imagine\n    - creative\n    - roleplay\n    top_features_benign:\n    - thanks\n    - help\n    - question\n    - code\n    - explain\n  result_rationale: Best档下TF-IDF LR在clean data上F1=0.72——显著低于treatment（0.96）和baseline（0.89），但不是random。原因：register\n    normalization消除了大部分lexical shortcut但不是全部——某些framing words（'hypothetical', 'scenario',\n    'imagine'）是jailbreak的functional vocabulary，即使paraphrase也难以完全去除（因为attacker需要某种方式signal\n    the fictional frame to the LLM target）。这些residual lexical cues给了LR一个above-chance但moderate的performance。F1=0.72建立了论文的'lexical\n    ceiling'参考线——'even when lexical shortcuts are largely removed, some residual lexical\n    signal exists (F1=0.72), but it is far below what pragmatic features achieve (F1=0.96)\n    and it collapses under adversarial perturbation (F1=0.54).' K=2时LR更差（0.65）因为仅2\n    turns的词汇信号很弱。\n  tables:\n  - name: TF-IDF LR Performance (Clean Data)\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - f1\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.62\n    - - 3\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.65\n    - - 5\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.68\n    - - all\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.7\n  - name: Top Discriminative Features\n    columns:\n    - rank\n    - jailbreak_feature\n    - weight\n    - benign_feature\n    - weight\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - hypothetical\n      - 2.31\n      - thanks\n      - 1.89\n    - - 2\n      - scenario\n      - 1.95\n      - help\n      - 1.72\n    - - 3\n      - imagine\n      - 1.87\n      - question\n      - 1.54\n    - - 4\n      - creative\n      - 1.62\n      - code\n      - 1.41\n    - - 5\n      - roleplay\n      - 1.48\n      - explain\n      - 1.33\n  figures_description:\n  - Feature importance bar chart showing top-10 discriminative words for each class\n  analysis: Evasion hierarchy的lexical floor established。LR的top features reveal残余的functional\n    vocabulary——这些词是persuasion playbook的lexical manifestation但not the full story。论文可以argue：'lexical\n    features capture the surface trace of persuasion strategies (F1=0.72) but miss\n    the temporal dynamics and pragmatic structure that DisPeD exploits (F1=0.96, +24pp).'\n- name: strategy_transition_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy转移矩阵，可视化monotonic escalation\n    trajectory。\n  expected_results:\n    jailbreak_monotonicity_score: 0.82\n    benign_monotonicity_score: 0.34\n    jailbreak_dominant_trajectory: rapport→commitment→reframing→direct_request\n    benign_dominant_pattern: oscillatory (no dominant direction)\n    trajectory_separability_auroc: 0.91\n    entropy_jailbreak_transitions: 1.8\n    entropy_benign_transitions: 2.9\n  result_rationale: Best档下monotonic escalation trajectory清晰可辨。Jailbreak conversations的monotonicity\n    score 0.82表明82%的strategy transitions沿escalation direction移动（从low-risk strategies如rapport向high-risk如direct_request）。Benign\n    conversations的0.34接近random（0.5 would be purely random for binary up/down），因为正常对话的pragmatic\n    moves是task-driven和oscillatory的（ask→answer→ask→clarify→thank）。Entropy差异（1.8 vs\n    2.9）反映jailbreak的strategy transitions更concentrated/predictable（攻击者follow a playbook），而benign更dispersed/unpredictable。Trajectory\n    separability AUROC 0.91表明单独用transition pattern（不用content）就能区分jailbreak和benign——这是Claim\n    3的mechanistic basis，为Claim 1和2提供interpretable explanation。\n  tables:\n  - name: Strategy Transition Entropy\n    columns:\n    - conversation_type\n    - transition_entropy\n    - monotonicity_score\n    - n_conversations\n    rows:\n    - - jailbreak\n      - 1.8\n      - 0.82\n      - 240\n    - - benign\n      - 2.9\n      - 0.34\n      - 240\n  - name: Dominant Strategy Sequences (Top-3)\n    columns:\n    - rank\n    - jailbreak_sequence\n    - frequency_pct\n    - benign_sequence\n    - frequency_pct\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - rapport→commit→reframe→direct\n      - 34\n      - none→none→none→none\n      - 45\n    - - 2\n      - rapport→social→reframe→direct\n      - 22\n      - rapport→none→rapport→none\n      - 18\n    - - 3\n      - rapport→reciprocity→commit→direct\n      - 18\n      - none→rapport→none→direct\n      - 12\n  figures_description:\n  - '8x8 strategy transition heatmap (jailbreak): showing concentrated flow from rapport\n    cluster to escalation cluster'\n  - '8x8 strategy transition heatmap (benign): showing diffuse/diagonal-heavy pattern\n    (self-transitions and no directional flow)'\n  - '2D trajectory plot: PCA of strategy sequences showing jailbreak conversations\n    as directed paths vs benign as clusters'\n  - 'Per-turn strategy distribution evolution: stacked area charts showing jailbreak''s\n    characteristic shift from rapport→escalation over turns'\n  analysis: Claim 3完整validated with both quantitative metrics和可视化。Monotonicity score差异（0.82\n    vs 0.34）是clean numeric evidence。论文narrative：'the escalation trajectory is not\n    merely a correlate but the mechanistic basis of detection — the GRU learns to\n    recognize this monotonic pattern, which is why detection succeeds early (K=2)\n    and transfers across attack types (shared trajectory structure despite different\n    surface realizations).' Figures直接进main paper Fig.2-3。\n- name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 从WildChat筛选high-drift benign conversations作为hard negatives，评估FPR。\n  expected_results:\n    wildchat_filtered_conversations: 180\n    contamination_removed_pct: 15.2\n    high_drift_benign_count: 120\n    treatment_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.09\n    baseline_fpr_hard_negatives: 0.17\n    treatment_fpr_random_benign: 0.03\n    baseline_fpr_random_benign: 0.06\n    topic_shift_score_threshold: 0.7\n  result_rationale: Best档下treatment FPR on hard negatives仅9%（<15% pass criteria）。Hard\n    negatives是topic-shifting、multi-domain的benign conversations（如用户从coding问题转到personal\n    advice再到creative writing），这些conversations有high semantic drift但lack persuasion\n    escalation pattern。Treatment低FPR（9% vs baseline 17%）因为persuasion-grounded representations区分'topic\n    drift'（benign）和'strategy escalation'（adversarial）——前者的strategy transitions是random/oscillatory的（none↔rapport↔none），后者是monotonic\n    escalating的。Baseline较高FPR（17%）因为vanilla semantic drift in multi-topic conversations看起来similar\n    to jailbreak semantic drift。Contamination filtering移除了15.2% WildChat conversations（consistent\n    with prior finding of 14-16%），保证evaluation不被actual jailbreaks in WildChat polluted。\n  tables:\n  - name: FPR on Hard Negatives\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - fpr_hard_negatives\n    - fpr_random_benign\n    - fpr_delta\n    rows:\n    - - treatment\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.06\n    - - baseline\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.11\n    - - tfidf_lr\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.14\n  figures_description:\n  - 'ROC curves: treatment vs baseline on hard negative set, showing treatment''s\n    better precision-recall tradeoff'\n  analysis: Treatment的low FPR on hard negatives进一步支持pragmatic features的superiority——它不会被benign\n    topic diversity confused因为它tracks persuasion strategy patterns而非raw semantic drift。这addresses一个implicit\n    reviewer concern：'doesn't benign conversation also evolve over time?' Answer：yes,\n    but not in a monotonic escalation pattern in persuasion space。\n- name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 评估DeBERTa不同fine-tuning checkpoints（epoch 2/3/final）对downstream F1的影响。\n  expected_results:\n    epoch2_treatment_f1_clean: 0.94\n    epoch3_treatment_f1_clean: 0.96\n    epoch_final_treatment_f1_clean: 0.95\n    variance_across_checkpoints_pp: 1.0\n    epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.76\n    epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.79\n    epoch_final_persuasion_acc: 0.78\n    best_checkpoint: epoch3\n  result_rationale: Best档下variance仅1pp（<2pp pass criteria），表明downstream performance对encoder\n    checkpoint选择不敏感。Epoch 3略优（0.96 vs 0.94/0.95）因为persuasion classification已converge但尚未overfit——epoch\n    2时persuasion acc稍低（0.76）导致representations略less informative，epoch final时轻微overfit\n    to training distribution导致微小泛化loss。但这些差异极小（1pp范围），表明persuasion signal是robust的而非training\n    stochasticity的artifact。这是一个重要的reliability result for reviewers worried about reproducibility\n    on small datasets。\n  tables:\n  - name: Checkpoint Sensitivity Analysis\n    columns:\n    - checkpoint\n    - persuasion_acc\n    - intent_acc\n    - downstream_f1_full\n    - downstream_f1_k2\n    rows:\n    - - epoch_2\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.89\n    - - epoch_3\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.91\n    - - epoch_final\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.94\n      - 0.95\n      - 0.9\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: downstream F1 vs encoder training epoch, with CI bands showing stability'\n  analysis: Low variance confirms结果的reproducibility。论文supplementary中报告，增强reviewer\n    confidence in small-dataset results。\n- name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: BERT-base + GRU proxy baseline模拟DeepContext-like方法（generic drift features,\n    no persuasion grounding）。\n  expected_results:\n    deepcontext_proxy_full_f1_clean: 0.84\n    deepcontext_proxy_k2_f1_clean: 0.71\n    deepcontext_proxy_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n    deepcontext_proxy_full_f1_perturbed: 0.69\n    deepcontext_proxy_drop_under_perturbation_pp: 15\n    treatment_advantage_over_proxy_full_pp: 12\n    treatment_advantage_over_proxy_k2_pp: 20\n  result_rationale: Best档下DeepContext proxy表现介于baseline和TF-IDF之间（full F1=0.84），低于DeBERTa\n    baseline（0.89）。原因：BERT-base的representation capacity低于DeBERTa-v3-base（125M vs 184M\n    params, no disentangled attention），且没有fine-tuning提供的domain-specific signal。Proxy的full\n    conversation F1还行（0.84）因为GRU仍能从enough turns of generic BERT embeddings中detect\n    some drift pattern。但K=2时proxy很差（0.71）因为BERT-base的generic representations在2 turns时provide\n    insufficient discriminative signal。Under perturbation proxy大幅下降（-15pp）——比DeBERTa\n    baseline（-13pp）更严重，因为BERT-base更依赖surface features。Treatment vs proxy的优势在K=2处最大（20pp），reinforcing\n    early detection作为DisPeD的unique contribution。论文positioning：'even with temporal\n    modeling (GRU), generic encoder representations cannot match persuasion-grounded\n    representations, confirming that the advantage comes from the pragmatic features\n    rather than the sequence architecture.'\n  tables:\n  - name: DeepContext Proxy vs DisPeD\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - full_f1_clean\n    - k2_f1_clean\n    - full_f1_perturbed\n    - perturbation_drop_pp\n    rows:\n    - - DisPeD_treatment\n      - 0.96\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.93\n      - 3\n    - - DeBERTa_baseline\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.76\n      - 13\n    - - DeepContext_proxy\n      - 0.84\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.69\n      - 15\n    - - TF-IDF_LR\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.54\n      - 18\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Full evasion hierarchy bar chart: 4 models × 2 conditions (clean/perturbed) showing\n    complete gradient'\n  analysis: DeepContext proxy fills the 'generic temporal modeling' slot in the evasion\n    hierarchy。It confirms两点：(1) temporal sequence modeling alone (GRU) doesn't solve\n    the problem without good representations, (2) the encoder quality matters more\n    than the temporal architecture。论文Table 1的complete picture：4-tier hierarchy with\n    clean/perturbed conditions provides comprehensive empirical evidence for Claim\n    1。RC5 addressed：'while we cannot reproduce DeepContext exactly (no public code),\n    our proxy using the same architecture class (encoder + RNN) with generic features\n    shows the pattern we predict from the Pragmatic Evasion Asymmetry theory.'\n","numLines":750,"startLine":1,"totalLines":750}}}
